The spectral theorem, Takagi factorization, complex triangle inequality,
Cauchy--Schwarz, finite-dimensional compactness, positive-kernel and
Choi/Kraus arguments are mature tools. Their applications to this
particular singular locus and original resource class produce the
additional consequences. The four-column sign frame is a constructive
cancellation device; it does not make atom decompositions canonical.
The proof of Takagi conventions in Lemma 4.1 is included for a
self-contained ordinary proof, not as a claim to have invented Takagi
factorization.

